        "important": true,
        "explanation_rich": "**The FSM state, written as one IF.** A mechanical timer has three discrete positions and one raw input — the angle of the knob. This rule lands the row in `Unwound` at 0°, `Full` at the upper stop, and `Partial` everywhere in between. Worked example: **Bessie** sits at 0° → `Unwound`; **Olive** at 120° (of 360°) → `Partial`; **Rufus** at 360° → `Full`. Turn Bessie's knob to 60° and the same row re-derives to `Partial` on the next read, in every substrate."
